  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Interactable
  text: Look
  triggerRange: 30
  isEnabled: 1
--- !u!114 &1508475877
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1508475874}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7d20f73aabcb4cfbaac49363662be3e1, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueController
  currentDialogueIndex: 0
  textStartOffset: 0
  dialogues:
  - texts:
    - The engraving on the wall is being imaged by some kind of machine.
    advanceDialogueIndex: 0
    canvasDelayOffset: 0
  - texts:
    - '<<// :: SPEECH SYNTHESIS HASH f92c69d0dcd5287367ced9b5d3d679792b2fdca408292e37c4f6ed76b825578c '
    - Hello. Do not be alarmed. I am Diamber. I am examining this symbol on the wall
      -- the <color=yellow>Glyph</color>.
    - A portion of the <color=yellow>Glyph</color> just experienced a sort of reaction.
      See how part of it is glowing?
    - It has never done this before, at least not under my observation, or in any
      of the histories.
    - ...
    - You activated the node here? That <color=#FF8CAB>Terminal</color> has been
      dormant since my construction. Quite a significant development.
    - Please, take this.
    advanceDialogueIndex: 1
    canvasDelayOffset: 0
  - texts:
    - I have given you a <color=yellow>Glyphstone</color>, a device of my own design.
      It is bound to the true <color=yellow>Glyph</color> via remote connection.
    - I have long suspected the <color=yellow>Glyph</color> to actually be a map
      of the Mountain. Your awakening of the <color=#FF8CAB>leylines</color> further
      supports this hypothesis.
    - If more <color=#FF8CAB>leylines</color> are activated, the <color=yellow>Glyph</color>
      will likely react further.
    - That <color=yellow>Glyphstone</color> should help you follow the <color=#FF8CAB>leylines</color>
      across the land.
    - I would be grateful for your contribution to my research.
    advanceDialogueIndex: 1
    canvasDelayOffset: 0
  - texts:
    - It is my directive to study this place.
    - I do not know why I was tasked to do so, or by whom. Such knowledge is unavailable.
      My own nature has become a mystery to me.
    - I am fortunate to be well constructed, in this place, shielded from the elements.
      I fear what fates other Silicants have faced.
    - If you find any information on such topics, it would please me to analyze it.
    advanceDialogueIndex: 1
    canvasDelayOffset: 0
  - texts:
    - If you wish to leave this place, the only way is further up the Mountain.
    - The <color=yellow>Glyphstone</color> will open the way. Good luck.
    - PSST! Dev here. If you are reading this, you have finished the playable demo.
      Thank you for playing. I love you.
    advanceDialogueIndex: 0
    canvasDelayOffset: 0
  DialogueName: 
  LookAtOverride: {fileID: 1698200599}
  CameraY: 0.3
  canvasDelay: 0
  cameraFollowOffsetLerp: 0
